WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.750
A messenger brings an old
host a letter: the war is won.

2
00:00:04.800 --> 00:00:09.670
The host is delighted: "A victory is
twice itself when the achiever brings home

3
00:00:09.720 --> 00:00:11.230
full numbers."

4
00:00:11.280 --> 00:00:12.910
Soldiers march in.

5
00:00:12.960 --> 00:00:16.590
Armour goes up on pegs;
masks come out for a dance.

6
00:00:16.640 --> 00:00:18.920
The fighting is over.

7
00:00:18.970 --> 00:00:20.580
Or is it?

8
00:00:20.630 --> 00:00:22.950
Comedies usually end with weddings.

9
00:00:23.000 --> 00:00:25.620
So why does this one start with a war?

10
00:00:25.670 --> 00:00:29.110
In this mission, you'll hear a
young soldier talk about love,

11
00:00:29.160 --> 00:00:30.890
fresh from the fighting.

12
00:00:30.940 --> 00:00:33.580
You'll listen closely to
how these lovers talk,

13
00:00:33.630 --> 00:00:35.820
and ask where their words come from.

14
00:00:35.870 --> 00:00:39.340
And you'll see how courtship worked
for Shakespeare's first audience,

15
00:00:39.390 --> 00:00:40.850
masks and all.

16
00:00:40.900 --> 00:00:44.750
Your mission: explain why
this comedy starts with a war.
